# SIR trust rests on byte digests. A line-ending conversion would change schema
# bytes on checkout and invalidate every catalog digest, so normalization is
# pinned to LF for all text rather than left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
* text=auto eol=lf

pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
contracts/generated/** linguist-generated

# Documentation origin snapshots carry supplied bytes that may use any line
# ending. The rule above would rewrite those bytes on commit and checkout, so
# the admitted digest could never be recovered again. The snapshot files hold
# their payload base64-encoded, and normalization is disabled for exactly that
# narrow path rather than through a repository-wide binary policy.
docs/documentation-snapshots/** -text
